WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.470
Sikhs believe every person
carries a spark of divine light.

2
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:05.860
Not only Sikhs.

3
00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:09.640
Every person, of any
religion, caste or sex,

4
00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:11.600
carries the same light.

5
00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:15.680
Yet look around: greed, anger, pride.

6
00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:19.710
Sikh teaching even names five
thieves that rob a person.

7
00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:25.330
So if a spark of God lives in everyone,
why do so many people act selfishly?

8
00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:28.740
In this mission, you'll meet
two ways of facing life:

9
00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:31.030
the manmukh, and the gurmukh.

10
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.760
Then you'll see why Sikhs
call the world good,

11
00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:36.430
and still warn against clinging to it.

12
00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:41.330
Your mission: explain why people with a
spark of God inside them can still act

13
00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:42.270
selfishly.
